      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes. it\u0027s accumulative. `virtmgr` keeps the `Vec` of callbacks and notify accordingly. (see: \nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/android/virtmgr/src/aidl.rs;l\u003d1557)\n\n`registerCallback` is already acculative -- `start()` registers client callback, and `create()` registers state callback.",
